nahhas-irab:28-28.t:
رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَلِوالِدَيَّ: with fatḥa on the yāʾ, because it is the yāʾ of the first person; kasra on it is not permissible, and it is the counterpart of بِمُصْرِخِيَّ [Ibrāhīm: 22]. Likewise the reading of whoever read «ولوالدي» [i.e. "wa-li-wālidī", singular];
and whoever reads «ولوالدي» may make the yāʾ quiescent or give it fatḥa. [Translator's note: the unvowelled text does not distinguish the two readings mentioned.] وَلِمَنْ دَخَلَ بَيْتِيَ مُؤْمِناً وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ: conjoined with the preposition repeated. وَالْمُؤْمِناتِ: conjoined without repeating the preposition. وَلا تَزِدِ الظَّالِمِينَ إِلَّا تَباراً: al-Farrāʾ said:
except straying; better than it is the view of Mujāhid: except destruction, derived from "al-tibr"; "tabartu al-shayʾa" and "tabbartuhu" mean I broke the thing.
